 wife from the touch of a second man like to his own wife.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.701,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-50-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3048006","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"288a1bcbebfae5be537de30089a95c5116a3195e6e919334d92f17e0906ded14","compact":"e25fa83edcad4a676ba3fdbfb786454113ff2a8a85af7c8fc61e908970e2b090","nasal":"e25fa83edcad4a676ba3fdbfb786454113ff2a8a85af7c8fc61e908970e2b090"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-48-7","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":48,"verse":7,"english":"How do you yourself being a monarch and engaged in the royal office of maintaining subjects, carry away by stealth another's wife? O you of mighty prowess, you should specially protect the wives of kings. Do you therefore control your base inclination of oppressing another's wife. A hero does never perform what bring calumny upon himself. It becometh every individual to save another's wife from the touch of a second man like to his own wife.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.912,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-50-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3048007","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"383803209e1ba3c134befbe2958121214ac2e4b91fd5e34b4db463ac35607d5b","compact":"4dfa30b25c3357ef6cf0db1e005614707562c271a5860ef4c6291b78521ea5fd","nasal":"4dfa30b25c3357ef6cf0db1e005614707562c271a5860ef4c6291b78521ea5fd"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-48-8","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":48,"verse":8,"english":"O son of Paulastya, at the instance of the king mild subjects perform many an action conducing to virtue, wealth and desire, though not mentioned in the Šāstras.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.887,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-50-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3048008","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a0b6ff0b4c646636ef9beba6649ecf6af8f55a555a3afb2196e3021883de2310","compact":"95cce1677549c98a6a55a01daee7d08e607fa31013e59b7412ebd35541f0cb04","nasal":"469ff7551a1c4ea91f1e81f0ad0a190bde0a89c70b8f1a9a0d1d2f08ee71f601"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-48-9","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":48,"verse":9,"english":"The king is the virtue, the king is the desire and the king is the prime jewel of all subjects. Virtue, desire or sin-every thing ariseth from the king.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-50-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3048009","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0f02466c205b273d929afbd05b8d91ad730b505e3014b73aa8f7c2634621ce3e","compact":"9a43e183880b6d96fb22b4a7c8590b924a8a07d70dc0038bf9e3357a7564b3c8","nasal":"9a43e183880b6d96fb22b4a7c8590b924a8a07d70dc0038bf9e3357a7564b3c8"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-48-10","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":48,"verse":10,"english":"O you the best of Rākṣasas, you are vicious and unsteady; how have you come by riches like to a sinner attaining to the abode of celestials?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.733,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-50-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3048010","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3aa1b91cd079195bd42c2ba44d12fdead123876cae10cf1a1c121981507ac383","compact":"b4c3c74738558bc1c6d64318b5be8f3153df00ee9c8b7321ddc49c88b1d07f6a","nasal":"b4c3c74738558bc1c6d64318b5be8f3153df00ee9c8b7321ddc49c88b1d07f6a"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-48-11","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":48,"verse":11,"english":"A vicious person can never relinquish his sinful habits—virtue does never reside in the abodes of impious persons.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.625,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-50-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3048011","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"da717755c4371614787b265ab9e400fab13b278d02615baead12461d2aabbfef","compact":"8f872c00dc559b91bb24f6eae3298bb90f8a87f28e5329297fc7076328664885","nasal":"8f872c00dc559b91bb24f6eae3298bb90f8a87f28e5329297fc7076328664885"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-48-12","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":48,"verse":12,"english":"The mighty and the virtuous-souled Rāma has committed nothing wrong in your city or your dominions. Why do you then commit wrong by him?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-50-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3048012","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"300313446f13cd397c272e22d208626c50bd8148a53156cc01f438c327503cee","compact":"1da28c2fa8e50c77821745ba80870508ec470b14c3bbdd7bcc7443aa0a419f67","nasal":"1da28c2fa8e50c77821745ba80870508ec470b14c3bbdd7bcc7443aa0a419f67"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-48-13","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":48,"verse":13,"english":"Khara of Janasthāna is highly wicked and if Rāma of blameless actions has killed him on Surpanakha's account how is he to blame? Why do you then carry away the wife of that lord of men?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-50-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3048013","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5629340539318b9a9ed2bc59d2ce3dcc8506d51305b6cb1f80f337f1dc755823","compact":"2120079ffa010a705a9a72919d2fb3da4d523e217b52f1caf3998f58f6a70efc","nasal":"2120079ffa010a705a9a72919d2fb3da4d523e217b52f1caf3998f58f6a70efc"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-48-14","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":48,"verse":14,"english":"Khara of Janasthāna is highly wicked and if Rāma of blameless actions has killed him on Surpanakha's account how is he to blame? Why do you then carry away the wife of that lord of men?","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.791,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-50-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3048014","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"309c977bc6841f43cacb31cdef69b4d70545f1ea229b3364412eaba6e6fc882c","compact":"b243689a4137f1fd59f496ef4197f9bea1a0647f5092bcfe381f9fc38e63f14c","nasal":"b243689a4137f1fd59f496ef4197f9bea1a0647f5092bcfe381f9fc38e63f14c"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-48-15","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":48,"verse":15,"english":"Do you soon leave off Vaidehī. Like to Indra burning down Vịtrāsura, Rāma, looking with his terrible eyes like flaming fire, shall reduce you to ashes.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-50-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3048015","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7b1fc64f8fc2a9c19122384229069c3ae32df17404a81e779da3e363b5ed76a0","compact":"d48a8622c2979babb5679f06df3adb73673ac5dbbc9d3d041148a4c718281a6e","nasal":"829aece3de7aa40eea2abef52624a6fb317894f1d1a534797f027a415f9144e0"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-48-16","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":48,"verse":16,"english":"Do you not understand that you have tied with cloth a virulent serpent? Do you not see that you have placed around your neck the noose of death?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-50-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3048016","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"24d4a924b12f263758d7f8cfee2a34b9359a0ce0c578ffb47eb6d4ef248bcee6","compact":"54da421bbb1e62e8c255c5ceb9898105a5b6f8bca579d6a10b0f63b3dd7fc3bc","nasal":"fc2e13ad66799d3eb0812c4013afe2e7a75cfd7845622dbea3a7efd5ff788388"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-48-17","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":48,"verse":17,"english":"It is always proper to carry such a weight as does not exhaust (him who carries); it is always proper to take such a food as does not cause illness.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.845,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-50-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3048017","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cad854da12cdc5e6fa1189e08b4181ddd522a8b66c30c7ae5def8a87c9f91da9","compact":"846641de9677a9546b0111717ea2901778245a8c7c393640bb6a912b0d02b654","nasal":"ab5c8555b4135508bc0335c3d223cafb78bce7692d07ad6760ea9e4a8f974711"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-48-18","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":48,"verse":18,"english":"Who engageth himself in such an action as does not confer virtue, fame or glory, but bring about physical affliction only?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.828,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-50-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3048018","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9bc475dec27c89547205593312b61bc84462a173fcb8c5f0958496f99f85065a","compact":"26d48b5e29d557ce15a75c8ea675d1b785d6e51a1b794d870879e51ddd6f864c","nasal":"26d48b5e29d557ce15a75c8ea675d1b785d6e51a1b794d870879e51ddd6f864c"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-48-19","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":48,"verse":19,"english":"O Rāvana, I am sixty thousand years old and have been administering regularly my ancestral kingdom.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.717,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-50-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3048019","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7ec79376b99a61dbbf66ad63387d3048cc8d99a654f5e70ec5cb600b72ea