e":{"sanskritLocator":"3048022","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"21e813f270461986ff181b8a00803e0f9702e28b6c3e7def9a36b7f6b2744453","compact":"9ab52e7b29f1ac4e74d2db3c13b80884c72e2164105c84b588889a210f4f0240","nasal":"9ab52e7b29f1ac4e74d2db3c13b80884c72e2164105c84b588889a210f4f0240"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-48-23","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":48,"verse":23,"english":"Soon shall Rāma clad in bark destroy you in the battle field, who had many a time and oft destroyed in conflict the celestials and Dānavas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.902,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-50-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3048023","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c585c4a77200b24bdb23ba59821a84ac533867a37b0fb2b6ba98f363c5dfb621","compact":"dd398b81c8cef76ed7ba520875af3eb48ead914f0802cfaee3f0d8eac56531be","nasal":"dd398b81c8cef76ed7ba520875af3eb48ead914f0802cfaee3f0d8eac56531be"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-48-24","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":48,"verse":24,"english":"These two princes Rāma and Lakşmaņa are at a distance, what shall I do now? O vile being, undoubtedly shall you, terrified, be destroyed by thein.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-50-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3048024","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e300f83c7a27e09ab3f6125ba6ee2e6bc209e7d41d99e42aaad529d687a92ec9","compact":"82ae1b939fca3a9569eab4d61ec11ff54ed18012ec2d7aeea7d7c94eec94482a","nasal":"82ae1b939fca3a9569eab4d61ec11ff54ed18012ec2d7aeea7d7c94eec94482a"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-48-25","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":48,"verse":25,"english":"Myself drawing my breath you shall not be able to carry away this beloved queen of Rāma, the pure-natured Sitä having eyes resembling lotuses.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.758,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-50-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3048025","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3a3c38d9146284f62c670277537baafbd3bb93e6ef5c18af5cf3ef99440887df","compact":"ebf5c4f952fbef330195cdf3bb5333153fbe20fafaef7a4673fe82a24d839467","nasal":"ebf5c4f952fbef330195cdf3bb5333153fbe20fafaef7a4673fe82a24d839467"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-48-26","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":48,"verse":26,"english":"It is my duty to do good to the high-souled Rāma and Dasaratha even at the sacrifice of my life.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-50-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3048026","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f200a4e2369737a0c3f4149c36f120b1eb9efbd1bff126933d5c5bb7777399b7","compact":"a32eda3eae871c7f95f22cdca387fe1dc1cc3d5c19c264977e5c0be407155328","nasal":"a32eda3eae871c7f95f22cdca387fe1dc1cc3d5c19c264977e5c0be407155328"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-48-27","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":48,"verse":27,"english":"It is my duty to do good to the high-souled Rāma and Dasaratha even at the sacrifice of my life. Do you stand, O ten-necked one. Behold for a moment. O Ravana, I shall throw you headlong from this car, like to a fruit from its stalk. O ranger of the night, even to my utmost might I will render you hospitality in encounter.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.5,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-50-24","DUTT-3-50-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3048027","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"677380ab1866863ad9dc02bf60b5407b5bae4d09e1361c6708bba4eb0e07baeb","compact":"36507832306833bfaaff089f105bffaffe3f9e0683d9610ca8026b332ed27441","na